WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.958 --> 00:00:36.375
<b>In this verse, Lord Krishna is describing the pure definition of renunciation and a renunciate.</b>

2
00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:37.916
<b>Lord Krishna says</b>

3
00:00:37.916 --> 00:00:42.458
<b>that the person who neither</b>
<b>hates the fruits of action</b>

4
00:00:42.458 --> 00:00:47.958
<b>nor desires to obtain them is a true renunciate.</b>

5
00:00:47.958 --> 00:00:54.291
<b>Freedom from bondage is attained only by </b>
<b>the renunciate who is not influenced by dualities.</b>

6
00:00:54.291 --> 00:00:55.958
<b>What are these dualities,</b>

7
00:00:55.958 --> 00:01:00.083
<b>and who becomes an eternal</b>
<b>renunciate by being free from them?</b>

8
00:01:00.083 --> 00:01:03.666
<b>Lord Krishna is unveiling this very distinction.</b>

9
00:01:08.458 --> 00:01:09.666
<b>In the previous verse,</b>

10
00:01:09.666 --> 00:01:13.416
<b>Lord Krishna, while comparing </b>
<b>renunciation and Karma Yoga,</b>

11
00:01:13.416 --> 00:01:16.041
<b>stated Karma Yoga to be better.</b>

12
00:01:16.041 --> 00:01:21.041
<b>Expanding on this knowledge, in this verse, </b>
<b>Lord Krishna is explaining</b>

13
00:01:21.041 --> 00:01:22.875
<b>what renunciation is …</b>

14
00:01:22.875 --> 00:01:26.583
<b>and who should be considered</b>
<b>an eternal renunciate.</b>

15
00:01:26.583 --> 00:01:28.000
<b> Happiness and sorrow,</b>

16
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.916
<b>attachment and aversion,</b>

17
00:01:29.916 --> 00:01:34.250
<b>hope for desire and fear of disappointment – </b>
<b>these are the dualities,</b>

18
00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:39.708
<b>meaning the opposite circumstances </b>
<b>in which most humans are bound.</b>

19
00:01:39.708 --> 00:01:43.958
<b>But a Karma Yogi is not bound by such dualities</b>

20
00:01:43.958 --> 00:01:50.750
<b>because he performs his actions without </b>
<b>being attached to the fruits, as a duty.</b>

21
00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:54.458
<b>One who neither craves the fruits of action,</b>

22
00:01:54.458 --> 00:01:59.208
<b>nor hates them when the </b>
<b>results are unfavorable – </b>

23
00:01:59.208 --> 00:02:04.583
<b>such a Karma Yogi can free</b>
<b>himself from the bondage of action</b>

24
00:02:04.583 --> 00:02:09.416
<b>and ultimately attains the state of true liberation.</b>

25
00:02:09.416 --> 00:02:13.250
<b>One who progresses on the path </b>
<b>of duty with a pure mind –</b>

26
00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:17.500
<b>adverse circumstances </b>
<b>cannot hurt such a person;</b>

27
00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:22.041
<b>only such a person is worthy </b>
<b>of being called a renunciate.</b>

28
00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:23.500
<b>Lord Krishna is saying</b>

29
00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:26.125
<b>that true renunciation is </b>
<b>not the abandonment of actions</b>

30
00:02:26.125 --> 00:02:30.541
<b>but the relinquishment of </b>
<b>attachment to the fruits of actions.</b>

31
00:02:30.541 --> 00:02:32.375
<b>With this perspective, you</b>

32
00:02:32.375 --> 00:02:38.666
<b>can attain liberation while living in this world, </b>
<b>performing all your duties.</b>

33
00:02:38.666 --> 00:02:42.750
<b>For this reason, this perspective is also practical.</b>

34
00:02:47.291 --> 00:02:51.625
<b>Change is the law of creation.</b>

35
00:02:51.625 --> 00:02:54.250
<b>There are day and night;</b>

36
00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:57.333
<b>seasons come and go.</b>

37
00:02:57.333 --> 00:03:03.583
<b>Then why do you get disturbed by ever-changing </b>
<b>circumstances from moment to moment?</b>

38
00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:06.791
<b>Why do you find yourself </b>
<b>feeling confined and restricted?</b>

39
00:03:06.791 --> 00:03:11.416
<b>You will have to accept one truth –</b>

40
00:03:11.416 --> 00:03:21.541
<b>by renouncing this world or your actions, </b>
<b>you will never attain liberation or peace.</b>

41
00:03:21.541 --> 00:03:23.041
<b>Because</b>

42
00:03:23.041 --> 00:03:28.041
<b>the cause of your bondage is not your actions</b>

43
00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:32.375
<b>but your attachment to</b>
<b>the results of those actions.</b>

44
00:03:32.375 --> 00:03:33.791
<b>For this reason,</b>

45
00:03:33.791 --> 00:03:43.583
<b>you become over-enthusiastic with good results </b>
<b>and sad and ineffective with bad results.</b>

46
00:03:43.583 --> 00:03:49.625
<b>When your mind is attached </b>
<b>to the fruits of your actions, then</b>

47
00:03:49.625 --> 00:03:51.875
<b>how is peace possible?</b>

48
00:03:51.875 --> 00:03:56.291
<b>If you bring a change in your perspective,</b>

49
00:03:56.291 --> 00:03:59.000
<b>consider your action as a duty,</b>

50
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:03.541
<b>and the fulfillment of duty as the purpose of life, </b>

51
00:04:03.541 --> 00:04:08.208
<b>then life's dualities will never </b>
<b>be able to disturb you.</b>

52
00:04:08.208 --> 00:04:14.208
<b>Free from life's ups and downs, </b>
<b>you will attain inner stability.</b>

53
00:04:14.208 --> 00:04:18.750
<b>Even while performing the </b>
<b>actions of your material life,</b>

54
00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:22.708
<b>you will be called an eternal renunciate.</b>

55
00:04:22.708 --> 00:04:26.666
<b>This very state will give you such inner peace</b>

56
00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:29.666
<b>that does not depend on any result</b>

57
00:04:29.666 --> 00:04:30.916
<b>because</b>

58
00:04:30.916 --> 00:04:33.083
<b>the purpose of your life</b>

59
00:04:33.083 --> 00:04:39.875
<b>is to move towards spirituality </b>
<b>while walking on your path of action.</b>

60
00:04:44.458 --> 00:04:47.083
<b>If you are a child,</b>

61
00:04:47.083 --> 00:04:51.666
<b>do you worry about your parents?</b>

62
00:04:51.666 --> 00:04:54.083
<b>And if you are an adult,</b>

63
00:04:54.083 --> 00:04:59.791
<b>do you live in constant worry for your children?</b>

64
00:04:59.791 --> 00:05:06.916
<b>You will say that the answers to </b>
<b>both questions are naturally 'yes.'</b>

65
00:05:06.916 --> 00:05:08.208
<b>Tell me,</b>

66
00:05:08.208 --> 00:05:14.458
<b>living in worry is considered </b>
<b>natural; what an irony this is.</b>

67
00:05:14.458 --> 00:05:19.250
<b>There should be so much strength in </b>
<b>familial love and relationships</b>

68
00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:24.541
<b>that they free every member </b>
<b>from all kinds of worries.</b>

69
00:05:24.541 --> 00:05:27.916
<b>This can be possible</b>

70
00:05:27.916 --> 00:05:33.916
<b>if you live in family life as a renunciate.</b>

71
00:05:33.916 --> 00:05:38.958
<b>This may not seem easy to you, </b>
<b>but yes,</b>

72
00:05:38.958 --> 00:05:41.875
<b>listen further.</b>

73
00:05:41.875 --> 00:05:44.708
<b>Renunciation does not at all mean</b>

74
00:05:44.708 --> 00:05:50.750
<b>that you have to give up your </b>
<b>relatives or your duties.</b>

75
00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:51.833
<b>Rather,</b>

76
00:05:51.833 --> 00:05:57.458
<b>if you perform every social duty with full devotion</b>

77
00:05:57.458 --> 00:05:59.166
<b>but</b>

78
00:05:59.166 --> 00:06:03.625
<b>have no attachment to its result,</b>

79
00:06:03.625 --> 00:06:10.541
<b>then even while living in a family, </b>
<b>you can live the life of a renunciate.</b>

80
00:06:10.541 --> 00:06:19.750
<b>Love and a sense of service towards </b>
<b>each other bind a family in relationships.</b>

81
00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:22.083
<b>Whether you are a mother, father,</b>

82
00:06:22.083 --> 00:06:22.958
<b>husband,</b>

83
00:06:22.958 --> 00:06:23.875
<b>wife,</b>

84
00:06:23.875 --> 00:06:26.791
<b>son, daughter, or sibling –</b>

85
00:06:26.791 --> 00:06:32.625
<b>in your every role, you have to give your best,</b>

86
00:06:32.625 --> 00:06:33.791
<b>but</b>

87
00:06:33.791 --> 00:06:40.958
<b>you should not have any attachment </b>
<b>to the result of your performed duty.</b>

88
00:06:40.958 --> 00:06:43.125
<b>As a parent,</b>

89
00:06:43.125 --> 00:06:45.125
<b>it is your duty</b>

90
00:06:45.125 --> 00:06:50.041
<b>to give proper education to your children, </b>
<b>to make them capable,</b>

91
00:06:50.041 --> 00:06:51.000
<b>but</b>

92
00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:56.875
<b>then how much progress they make in</b>
<b>whichever profession they go into –</b>

93
00:06:56.875 --> 00:07:02.916
<b>you have no right to this result.</b>

94
00:07:02.916 --> 00:07:10.125
<b>If you perform your duties as a</b>
<b>renunciate while living in a family,</b>

95
00:07:10.125 --> 00:07:17.166
<b>you will find that such a true intimacy</b>
<b>will be born among family members</b>

96
00:07:17.166 --> 00:07:23.416
<b>in which there will be no place for worry or unrest.</b>

97
00:07:27.916 --> 00:07:34.416
<b>When you wake up in the morning</b>
<b>and leave for your business,</b>

98
00:07:34.416 --> 00:07:37.375
<b>what are you thinking?</b>

99
00:07:37.375 --> 00:07:41.583
<b>Are you hopeful for a new day,</b>

100
00:07:41.583 --> 00:07:43.958
<b>or are you scared and nervous,</b>

101
00:07:43.958 --> 00:07:49.708
<b>just wanting to get through today </b>
<b>and see about tomorrow?</b>

102
00:07:49.708 --> 00:07:57.375
<b>If you remain disorganized between </b>
<b>two opposite situations in your business,</b>

103
00:07:57.375 --> 00:08:04.791
<b>the main reason is your attachment </b>
<b>to the results of your work.</b>

104
00:08:04.791 --> 00:08:07.291
<b>You may question that</b>

105
00:08:07.291 --> 00:08:11.833
<b>everything depends on the result.</b>

106
00:08:11.833 --> 00:08:21.416
<b>The outcome of your work will determine </b>
<b>your professional livelihood or progress.</b>

107
00:08:21.416 --> 00:08:23.666
<b>You are not thinking incorrectly.</b>

108
00:08:23.666 --> 00:08:29.458
<b>Just extend this thinking a little further.</b>

109
00:08:29.458 --> 00:08:34.958
<b>Whatever you do, results are inevitable.</b>

110
00:08:34.958 --> 00:08:36.000
<b>But</b>

111
00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:38.000
<b>it is not necessary to always </b>
<b>remain unbalanced</b>

112
00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:44.166
<b>between the elation of success </b>
<b>and the disappointment of failure.</b>

113
00:08:44.166 --> 00:08:48.916
<b>Do your work with full devotion and effort.</b>

114
00:08:48.916 --> 00:08:54.541
<b>Just stop worrying about its good or bad results.</b>

115
00:08:54.541 --> 00:09:01.250
<b>In this state of equanimity, you will always</b>
<b>find yourself full of self-confidence.</b>

116
00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:03.916
<b>Take an example.</b>

117
00:09:03.916 --> 00:09:07.500
<b>It's a situation of extreme pressure,</b>

118
00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:15.125
<b>and the future of the entire organization depends </b>
<b>on the decisive opinion of a high-ranking official.</b>

119
00:09:15.125 --> 00:09:18.875
<b>If this official worries about the result,</b>

120
00:09:18.875 --> 00:09:22.083
<b>then there is a strong possibility that</b>

121
00:09:22.083 --> 00:09:29.791
<b>a decision made in nervousness or urgency </b>
<b>may prove disastrous for the organization.</b>

122
00:09:29.791 --> 00:09:33.166
<b>But if that high-ranking official</b>

123
00:09:33.166 --> 00:09:41.833
<b>makes a decision based on facts and logic without</b>
<b>worrying about the result, being devoid of emotion,</b>

124
00:09:41.833 --> 00:09:45.583
<b>then the possibility of a successful </b>
<b>outcome also increases.</b>

125
00:09:45.583 --> 00:09:51.625
<b>Attachment to the result casts </b>
<b>a haze of uncertainty,</b>

126
00:09:51.625 --> 00:09:57.250
<b>whereas clarity comes in a state of equanimity.</b>

127
00:09:57.250 --> 00:10:04.500
<b>Only your actions and your </b>
<b>perspective are in your control;</b>

128
00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:09.083
<b>you have no control over the result.</b>

